%erg 0.1
Title: Add a gofmt + go vet adherence ratchet to the test suite
Created: 2026-06-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-03T03:35Z claude created
2026-06-03T05:10Z claude note corrected the root cause: the version.go "drift" is STOCK gofmt doc-comment smart-quoting ('' -> U+201D, two backticks -> U+201C; proposal #51082, Go 1.19+), NOT a corrupt/broken/padme toolchain. Refs golang/go#61365, #76975.
2026-06-03T06:00Z claude note policy decided (author): STOP fighting gofmt -- relax the ASCII guard to ALLOW U+201C/U+201D in *.go only (embedded assets *.md/.ergrc stay strictly ASCII), so gofmt and the guard no longer conflict. Plus (advisor): reword version.go's shellSingleQuote comment so a comment ABOUT quote-escaping does not itself get smart-quoted into misdocumentation -- the policy is the forward guard, the reword keeps this one doc true. Net: production tree ends with ZERO smart quotes; the allowlist + negative controls protect future gofmt runs.

--- body ---
## Context

git-erg has no mechanical Go-formatting/vet gate -- the analog of the Python
ruff adherence check the harness rules mandate. `make check` runs the suite +
corpus validation but never `gofmt -l` or `go vet`, so formatting drift only
gets caught by a human reviewer or /verify's ad-hoc pass. The /verify on PR
#242 (ticket 0207) flagged this gap directly.

Why a plain ratchet could not just be added: gofmt's doc-comment formatter
applies Markdown-style smart quotes -- `''` -> U+201D, two backticks -> U+201C
-- in every Go >= 1.19 (proposal #51082; golang/go#61365, #76975). So a real
gofmt on ANY machine (CI included) wants to rewrite version.go's `'\''`
comment to a non-ASCII glyph, which the ASCII-only src/go guard (0167) rejects.
This is stock gofmt behaviour, not a broken toolchain.

Policy decision (author): stop fighting gofmt -- relax the ASCII guard to allow
exactly U+201C and U+201D in *.go (the two glyphs gofmt emits), keeping the
embedded assets strictly ASCII. Both glyphs are printing, non-control,
non-bidi, non-invisible and cannot appear in Go identifiers, so the
Trojan-Source surface (CVE-2021-42574) is not reopened.

## Actions

1. Relax `tests/test_encoding.sh`: in the `*.go` branch, strip U+201C/U+201D
   before flagging non-ASCII; `*.md` and `.ergrc` stay strictly ASCII. Add
   negative controls: em-dash in .go still rejected; U+201D in .go allowed;
   U+201D in a .md asset still rejected (proves the branches did not collapse).
2. Reword `src/go/version.go`'s shellSingleQuote comment so it does not contain
   the literal `''` pair -- it documents quote-escaping and must stay accurate,
   not be smart-quoted into nonsense. (Policy still allows the glyph elsewhere;
   this keeps one doc true and gofmt-stable.)
3. Run a real `gofmt -w src/go/` to fix genuine formatting drift (ref_test.go,
   refs_test.go). After step 2 it introduces no smart quotes; confirm
   `grep -RP '[^\x00-\x7F]' src/go` is empty.
4. Add `tests/test_gofmt.sh` (gofmt -l clean + `go vet ./...` clean, with a
   non-vacuous mis-indent negative control); register `gofmt` in TEST_SUITES.
5. Document the scoped exception in docs/threat-model.md (Controls).

## Test

`tests/test_gofmt.sh` (mis-indented temp .go is flagged by gofmt -l) and the
three new `tests/test_encoding.sh` controls.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] test_encoding allows U+201C/U+201D in *.go ONLY; *.md/.ergrc strict;
      three negative controls pass (em-dash rejected, smart-quote allowed in
      .go, smart-quote rejected in asset).
- [ ] version.go's shellSingleQuote comment reworded; `grep -RP '[^\x00-\x7F]'
      src/go` is empty (zero smart quotes in the production tree).
- [ ] `gofmt -l src/go/` clean; `go vet ./...` clean.
- [ ] `tests/test_gofmt.sh` exists, registered in TEST_SUITES, non-vacuous.
- [ ] docs/threat-model.md documents the scoped exception + assets-stay-strict.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
